Fix two defects of `--boogie /typeEncoding:m`, through the Boogie that Dafny builds against: a labeled assertion assumed through a quantifier that binds nothing made the solver reject the whole program, where `:a` verifies it; and `hide *` hid no definition of a generic function, so the solver got every instance of those definitions, which made proofs of the standard library run out of resources; the default `/typeEncoding:a` is unchanged
